  "source_route": [
    "Reuse scalar image-length subadditivity and the existing Fubini theorem on actual compact linear images to prove every-row volume subadditivity.",
    "Reuse polar projection factorization, normal Jacobians and exterior Hadamard bounds to obtain a relative projection-volume modulus uniform over all compact convex bodies.",
    "Use independent normalized-profile laws before existence. Compactness and full probability support give a common positive ball-mass floor; the existing superlevel-root theorem gives a uniform finite-p lower factor.",
    "Reuse the original open/closed convex construction equality. Compare bounded generators at finite cutoffs, then use positive natural-root limits, normalized measure monotonicity and the existing extended contraction squeeze at infinity.",
    "Reuse the existing logarithmic norm convexity and corrected reciprocal secant for a symmetric exp(C|p-q|) comparison at finite exponents, with separate zero-supremum branches.",
    "Reuse full scalar norm continuity for projection-beta convergence. Positive normalization, a multiplicative extended-real sandwich and existing countable-base topology give the full extended-exponent continuity theorem."
  ],
  "coverage_qualification": "This closes exponent continuity in 3.2.45, including arbitrary target sets, degree zero as a supporting extension, one and infinity, and zero or infinite masses. The printed quantitative estimate remains refuted. Full mixed-volume section comparisons, the sharp Q_infinity <= Q_1 refinement and Gillespie section/product theorems remain pending. Explicit user deferrals are preserved.",
